# Photograph the sneak-attack gate for a rogue's FIRST blow from Improved
# Invisibility in MELEE against a victim that has Blind-Fight. Part of bead
# inc-nkf2.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-sneak-invis.dat \
#   INCURSION_SNEAK_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sneak-invis-blindfight.keys <seed>
#
# Read the result with tools/check_sneak_invis.sh (case D).
#
# THE POINT. Blind-Fight protects only against a MELEE unseen attacker (SRD),
# so in melee the unseen-surprise branch at src/Fight.cpp:4152 must stay off
# entirely: the probe's "pre" line must read actUnseen=0 and surprise=0. This
# is the green guard that the ranged case C must NOT borrow Blind-Fight's
# protection through.
#
# THE VICTIM is the same green hag as tools/keys/sneak-invis-ranged.keys:
# FT_BLIND_FIGHT, SZ_MEDIUM, no M_SEE_INVIS, CA_INFRAVISION. The rogue casts
# Improved Invisibility before summoning, so the summon does not break it and
# the first blow is from invisibility. The hag is summoned one square east so
# the rogue's knife swing is a MELEE attack (walking into it), unlike the
# throw in the ranged script.
#
# No light spell is needed: the unlit arrival room plus the hag's infravision
# is the configuration the ranged script already explains.
#
# The victim is freshly summoned and therefore flat-footed; case D asserts
# only the "pre" fields actUnseen=0 and surprise=0, which flat-footedness does
# not touch.

@include sneak-invis-chargen.keys

SPACE   # dismiss the arrival-room description

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE   # Cheat Death
DOWN*7
SPACE   # Infinite Mana
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Improved Invisibility" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

# Cast Improved Invisibility on the rogue first, so the blow below is the
# first blow after the cast.
m
@cursorto:mark "Improved Invisibility" DOWN
ENTER
*
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@dump:cast

# Summon the green hag one square east.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Hags"
@choose "green hag"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:victim

# The measured blow: step east into the hag and swing the knife in melee.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:melee-strike

@quit
